#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092261 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092118 :question/id #uuid "775dfc95-df31-5198-aeb2-4603b8386957" :question/math-academy-id "e-728" :question/problem "Given that $y= 3\\cdot 2^{1 - x},$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny = 3\\cdot 2^u, \\qquad u=1-x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} = 3\\cdot 2^u\\ln(2),\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} =-1.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {2}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {2}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {2}^{1-x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f4bfd24-dafd-57b3-940a-154a6e0acf3d" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186657656 :question-generator/id #uuid "e38a7c7e-4f5a-5d38-a6c1-7f2505ccfb41" :question-generator/script "generators/44/442d0e4b1af6a2ef291083bde6a9a87e6d87c5ed2c583197e098c1ca53341021/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092733 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d9ee625-e773-554a-b6fd-1b00c950d2f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\cdot 3^{2x}\\ln (3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090599} {:answer/id #uuid "a2e4f469-6799-5ce4-b565-a59f324b5ec8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x3^{2x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090600} {:answer/id #uuid "bdacec05-5c20-55b6-8105-e82bd5158002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x3^{2x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090601} {:answer/id #uuid "f7139b42-c4a4-5c78-ab9a-4c8bcf3ecb8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x3^{2x^{2}}\\ln (3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090602} {:answer/i