frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}={3}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={3}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)\\cdot (4x) \\\\  & =4x\\cdot {3}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\  & =4x\\cdot {3}^{2{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092735 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa029f20-9e8b-5be2-9aaf-e25b51c039d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(12x)3^{6x^{2} - 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090611} {:answer/id #uuid "adc2037a-76a7-570a-a5b0-aad7e20b5c7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(12x)3^{6x^{2} - 4}\\ln (3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090612} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe2a81f-2507-5d07-bb73-29c3696d08a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(12x - 4)3^{6x^{2} - 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090613} {:answer/id #uuid "d255dee3-7ee2-5cfc-af90-221a41a1961e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(12x - 4)3^{6x^{2} - 4}\\ln (3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090614} {:answer/id #uuid "582b9da7-3b84-58f5-a115-eedbe6fbcb2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(12x^{3})3^{12x}\\ln (3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090615}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d7d3b7cd-8fef-5ba2-8969-6b86fbad9f15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090610}] :question/id #uuid "475f4a17-648a-5df1-a5af-24c4bc3218f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-48631" :question/problem "Given that $y = 3^{6x^{2} - 4}$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233099 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b5b538e-387a-5bc3-9ad6-828140780508" :question/math-academy-id "q-107458" :question/problem "If $f(x)={2}^{3-{x}^{3}},$ find ${f}^{'}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={2}^{u},\\,u=3-{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}={2}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}2,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={2}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}2\\cdot (-3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-3{x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}2 \\\\  & =-3{x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{3-{x}^{3}}\\operatorname{ln}2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234314 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc156fa4-1ae1-5983-b7ca-740de211698e" :question/math-academy-id "q-71881" :question/problem "Given that $y=2\\cdot {5}^{x+{x}^{3}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=2\\cdot {5}^{u},\\,u=x+{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=2\\cdot {5}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}5,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1+3{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {5}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}5\\cdot (1+3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =(1+3{x}^{2})\\cdot 2\\cdot {5}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}5 \\\\  & =(2+6{x}^{2}){5}^{x+{x}^{3}}\\operatorname{ln}5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244059 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "152cb325-9ed7-57e6-9c36-b431d68cdffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\cdot {4}^{{x}^{2}-1}ln⁡4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241362} {:answer/id #uuid "2e76f4b9-59bb-51c9-a297-586eb211cb2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x\\cdot {4}^{{x}^{2}-1}ln⁡4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241592} {:answer/id #uuid "33d1a60d-2b25-5917-b2e1